   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**National governments pay more for heritage than local ones in 30 of the 37 countries that report both.**\n\nLocal governments spend more in 7 countries, most of all in Belgium, where towns and cities supply **88%** of national and local heritage spending.\n\nThe dashboard ranks every country by the local share. Each country's latest year from 2020–2024 with both figures; regional governments are left out. Source: UIS, February 2026 release; indicators HEXPCSTPPPCAPGOV.NTL.HER.PU, HEXPCSTPPPCAPGOV.LOC.HER.PU.",
